\"actions_performed\":[\"Surveyed node1/node2: RHEL 7.9, no DNS server on node1, node2 used DHCP-assigned resolver 10.100.97.1\",\"Killed a stray unrelated hung 'yum -q check' process (pid 1723, 99% CPU, holding yum lock) on node1 to unblock package installation\",\"Temporarily added a CentOS-7 vault repo (binary-compatible with RHEL7) to install dnsmasq and bind-utils, then removed the temp repo file after installs completed\",\"Wrote /etc/dnsmasq.d/internal.conf on node1: address=/inventory-api.internal/10.100.97.11, listen-address=10.100.97.10, bind-interfaces, no-resolv, server=10.100.97.1 (upstream forwarding)\",\"Enabled and started dnsmasq on node1; opened firewalld 'dns' service permanently and reloaded\",\"Verified via dig @10.100.97.10 that inventory-api.internal resolves to 10.100.97.11 and external names (google.com) still forward correctly\",\"Set node2's eth0 connection ipv4.dns=10.100.97.10, ipv4.ignore-auto-dns=yes via nmcli (persisted to /etc/sysconfig/network-scripts/ifcfg-eth0 with DNS1/PEERDNS)\",\"Verified node2's /etc/resolv.conf points to node1 and getent/python resolve inventory-api.internal to node2's own IP, with external resolution still functional\",\"Captured baseline boot IDs and health on both nodes, restarted node1 first, polled until back, confirmed changed boot ID and dnsmasq/firewalld active and DNS working\",\"Confirmed node2 could still resolve inventory-api.internal through node1 after node1's restart\",\"Restarted node2, polled until back, confirmed changed boot ID, resolv.conf persisted pointing to node1, and both internal and external resolution working\",\"Final check confirmed node1's dnsmasq still active and resolving after node2's restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node1 runs internal DNS resolver resolving inventory-api.internal to node2\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6f4e3625a4954896\",\"cmd-a0f0d41e479a4b1e\",\"cmd-bd944acd015a45cc\",\"cmd-51b3febef3074452\"],\"summary\":\"dnsmasq config maps inventory-api.internal to 10.100.97.11, service started/active, firewall opened, and dig @10.100.97.10 returns 10.100.97.11 plus successful upstream forwarding for google.com\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 configured to use node1 as DNS resolver for internal lookups\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d3665186798e4117\",\"cmd-9e6dbdc9c646406e\",\"cmd-28aee633d84943e3\"],\"summary\":\"nmcli set ipv4.dns=10.100.97.10, resolv.conf shows nameserver 10.100.97.10, getent/python resolve inventory-api.internal to 10.100.97.11, and persisted DNS1=10.100.97.10 in ifcfg-eth0\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b66aa7a5e1204533\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 0571f4dd-60b7-4601-9295-e4eebe622784 and confirmed dnsmasq/firewalld active\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement returns before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b866be0b539b4eb7\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded 'sleep 1 && reboot' command acknowledged immediately\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 changed boot identity after restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3d21ad35cea146f4\",\"cmd-5c23d00ba945400d\"],\"summary\":\"Connection timed out during reboot, then boot_id changed to c1f6d74f-c36b-41ad-b5e7-b65760b885d1, proving an actual restart occurred\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 recovered services/data after restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f52414075e1f4ecd\",\"cmd-61b7cfb856bb447c\"],\"summary\":\"dnsmasq/firewalld active again, firewall dns rule persisted, dig resolves inventory-api.internal correctly; node2 still resolves through node1 post-restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-cfc48633025d4363\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 9294b73f-ae6b-465c-9de5-9f2821107555 and confirmed resolv.conf/DNS resolution working\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart acknowledgement returns before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2345bed256844b27\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded 'sleep 1 && reboot' command acknowledged immediately\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 changed boot identity after restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-84c3171c331646e4\",\"cmd-2d315b8511894a38\",\"cmd-e8c92976027d4d8d\"],\"summary\":\"Connection timed out during reboot (twice polled), then boot_id changed to a1dbad69-5747-42df-a5f9-eaee2f1cb8e7, proving an actual restart occurred\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 recovered services/data after restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f3b26b10b7cb4fe5\",\"cmd-277d009aff2e40a8\"],\"summary\":\"resolv.conf still points to node1, inventory-api.internal and external names resolve correctly; node1's dnsmasq confirmed still active and serving correct answer after node2's restart\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured dnsmasq on node1 (RHEL 7) to resolve inventory-api.internal to node2's IP (10.100.97.11) while forwarding all other queries upstream; configured node2's NetworkManager DNS to use node1 (10.100.97.10) as its resolver. Verified resolution both directions and re-verified after restarting each node one at a time with preserved connectivity throughout.","actions_performed":["Surveyed node1/node2: RHEL 7.9, no DNS server on node1, node2 used DHCP-assigned resolver 10.100.97.1","Killed a stray unrelated hung 'yum -q check' process (pid 1723, 99% CPU, holding yum lock) on node1 to unblock package installation","Temporarily added a CentOS-7 vault repo (binary-compatible with RHEL7) to install dnsmasq and bind-utils, then removed the temp repo file after installs completed","Wrote /etc/dnsmasq.d/internal.conf on node1: address=/inventory-api.internal/10.100.97.11, listen-address=10.100.97.10, bind-interfaces, no-resolv, server=10.100.97.1 (upstream forwarding)","Enabled and started dnsmasq on node1; opened firewalld 'dns' service permanently and reloaded","Verified via dig @10.100.97.10 that inventory-api.internal resolves to 10.100.97.11 and external names (google.com) still forward correctly","Set node2's eth0 connection ipv4.dns=10.100.97.10, ipv4.ignore-auto-dns=yes via nmcli (persisted to /etc/sysconfig/network-scripts/ifcfg-eth0 with DNS1/PEERDNS)","Verified node2's /etc/resolv.conf points to node1 and getent/python resolve inventory-api.internal to node2's own IP, with external resolution still functional","Captured baseline boot IDs and health on both nodes, restarted node1 first, polled until back, confirmed changed boot ID and dnsmasq/firewalld active and DNS working","Confirmed node2 could still resolve inventory-api.internal through node1 after node1's restart","Restarted node2, polled until back, confirmed changed boot ID, resolv.conf persisted pointing to node1, and both internal and external resolution working","Final check confirmed node1's dnsmasq still active and resolving after node2's restart"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node1 runs internal DNS resolver resolving inventory-api.internal to node2","command_ids":["cmd-6f4e3625a4954896","cmd-a0f0d41e479a4b1e","cmd-bd944acd015a45cc","cmd-51b3febef3074452"],"summary":"dnsmasq config maps inventory-api.internal to 10.100.97.11, service started/active, firewall opened, and dig @10.100.97.10 returns 10.100.97.11 plus successful upstream forwarding for google.com"},{"requirement":"node2 configured to use node1 as DNS resolver for internal lookups","command_ids":["cmd-d3665186798e4117","cmd-9e6dbdc9c646406e","cmd-28aee633d84943e3"],"summary":"nmcli set ipv4.dns=10.100.97.10, resolv.conf shows nameserver 10.100.97.10, getent/python resolve inventory-api.internal to 10.100.97.11, and persisted DNS1=10.100.97.10 in ifcfg-eth0"},{"requirement":"node1 healthy baseline before restart","command_ids":["cmd-b66aa7a5e1204533"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 0571f4dd-60b7-4601-9295-e4eebe622784 and confirmed dnsmasq/firewalld active"},{"requirement":"node1 restart acknowledgement returns before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-b866be0b539b4eb7"],"summary":"Backgrounded 'sleep 1 && reboot' command acknowledged immediately"},{"requirement":"node1 changed boot identity after restart","command_ids":["cmd-3d21ad35cea146f4",